  q(INF,'After a needlestick, what should the medical assistant do right away?','Wash the area with soap and water and report the exposure',['Ignore it if there is no bleeding','Squeeze the site and apply bleach','Wait until the end of the shift to report it'],'B','Prompt reporting allows testing and preventive treatment if needed.',BLESI),
  q(SPEC,'How long should a serum separator tube sit before centrifuging?','About 30 minutes, to let the blood clot',['No time, centrifuge immediately','About 5 seconds','About 8 hours'],'C','Spinning before clotting produces a poor serum sample that may contain fibrin strands.',BLESI),
  q(SPEC,'Which tube contains heparin and is often used for chemistry tests on plasma?','Green top',['Red top','Light blue top','Gray top'],'D','Heparin prevents clotting by blocking thrombin, so plasma can be separated right away.',BLESI),
  q(SPEC,'Where is a heel puncture done on an infant?','On the outer edges of the bottom of the heel',['In the center of the heel’s back curve','On the arch of the foot','On the big toe'],'A','Avoiding the center of the heel reduces the risk of injuring the heel bone.',BLESI),
  q(SPEC,'Which simple test checks a child for pinworms?','Pressing clear tape around the anus in the morning',['A throat swab taken at noon and sent to the lab for culture','A urine dipstick at bedtime','A finger stick at any time'],'B','Pinworm eggs are laid around the anus at night and collected before bathing.',BLESI),
  q(SPEC,'What type of container is needed for a urine culture?','A sterile container',['Any clean kitchen jar','A paper cup','A container with a preservative for blood'],'C','A sterile container prevents contamination that could cause a false result.',BLESI),
  q(DX,'An ECG tracing drifts up and down across the paper. What often causes this wandering baseline?','Loose electrodes or patient movement',['A normal heart rhythm','A heart attack in progress','Correct lead placement'],'D','Check the electrodes and have the patient lie still and breathe normally.',BLESI),
  q(DX,'What total cholesterol level is generally considered desirable for adults?','Below 200 mg/dL',['Above 300 mg/dL','Exactly 250 mg/dL','Below 50 mg/dL'],'A','LDL, HDL and triglycerides are also part of a lipid panel, usually drawn after fasting.',BLESI),
  q(DX,'What does urine specific gravity measure?','How concentrated the urine is',['The urine’s color only','The number of bacteria','The amount of protein'],'B','High specific gravity may suggest dehydration; low may suggest overhydration.',BLESI),
  q(DX,'Which test records the heart’s activity while the patient walks on a treadmill?','A cardiac stress test',['A Holter monitor','A Jaeger card','A spirometry test'],'C','Stress tests show how the heart responds to exercise and can reveal blocked arteries.',BLESI),
  q(DX,'Which device tests hearing by playing tones at different pitches and volumes?','An audiometer',['An otoscope','A tonometer','An ophthalmoscope'],'D','Audiometry results are shown on an audiogram, which graphs hearing at each pitch.',BLESI),
  q(CLIN,'Where are eye drops placed?','In the lower conjunctival sac',['Directly on the cornea','In the inner corner of the eye only','On the upper eyelid'],'A','The patient looks up while the lower lid is gently pulled down.',BLESI),
  q(CLIN,'Why is the dorsogluteal site usually avoided for intramuscular injections?','It is close to the sciatic nerve',['It has too little muscle in adults','It absorbs medicine too quickly','It is too easy to reach'],'B','The ventrogluteal site is preferred for adults because it is away from large nerves and vessels.',BLESI),
  q(CLIN,'A blood pressure cuff that is too small for the arm can cause which error?','A falsely high reading',['A falsely low reading','No reading at all','An accurate reading'],'C','Cuff width should be about 40% of the arm’s circumference; a cuff too large reads falsely low.',BLESI),
  q(CLIN,'Which treatment uses extreme cold, such as liquid nitrogen, to destroy warts?','Cryosurgery',['Electrocautery','Laser therapy','Ultrasound therapy'],'D','The treated area may blister and then heal over 1 to 2 weeks.',BLESI),
  q(CLIN,'Why is a cold compress used in the first 24 to 48 hours after a sprain?','To reduce swelling and pain',['To increase blood flow to the area','To speed up bruising','To soften the skin'],'A','Heat may be used later to relax muscles and improve circulation.',BLESI),
  q(EXAM,'In semi-Fowler’s position, the head of the table is raised to about what angle?','About 30 to 45 degrees',['About 90 degrees','Flat at 0 degrees','About 180 degrees'],'B','Semi-Fowler’s is used for patients with breathing problems who cannot sit fully upright.',BLESI),
  q(EXAM,'Which exam method moves a patient’s joints to check range of motion?','Manipulation',['Auscultation','Inspection','Mensuration'],'C','Manipulation is passive movement of a joint by the examiner to check its range of motion.',BLESI),
  q(EXAM,'Why are a child’s height and weight plotted on a growth chart?','To compare growth with other children of the same age and sex',['To decide the child’s blood type and the safest donor for a transfusion','To diagnose a heart condition','To check the child’s vision'],'D','Percentiles show how a child’s size compares and whether growth is on track.',BLESI),
  q(EXAM,'Blood pressure and pulse are measured lying, sitting and standing. What are these called?','Orthostatic vital signs',['Apical vital signs','Baseline vital signs','Pediatric vital signs'],'A','A drop in blood pressure on standing can suggest dehydration or medication effects.',BLESI),
  q(EXAM,'To screen for scoliosis, how is the patient usually positioned?','Bending forward at the waist with arms hanging',['Lying flat on the back','Lying on the left side','Sitting with legs crossed'],'B','The Adams forward bend test makes a curve or rib hump easier to see.',BLESI)
